%S A123437 1,2,4,11,33,146,848,6880,68743,778449,9452620,121121755,1642823955
%N A123437 Number of opposition perfect graphs on n nodes.
%C A123437 Graphs whose edges can be oriented so that in every induced path on 4 vertices the two end edges either both point inwards or both point outwards. All such graphs are perfect, as per the Strong Perfect Graph Theorem (Hougardy, 2006). - _Meghanto Majumder_, Sep 29 2026
%H A123437 S. Hougardy, <a href="http://www.or.uni-bonn.de/~hougardy/">Home Page</a>
%H A123437 S. Hougardy, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.disc.2006.05.021">Classes of perfect graphs</a>, Discr. Math. 306 (2006), 2529-2571.
%Y A123437 Cf. A000088, A052431 (perfect graphs), A123405, A123459 (strict opposition graphs).
%K A123437 nonn,more,changed
%O A123437 1,2
